From 3485cf0949f14e53f6a744098abf4ccc09cf3e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kyehn <kyehn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 05:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] agent: enforce the configured window; converge must-free
 folds below it

The gateway can prove more headroom than a conservative configured window
(e.g. 1048576 reported vs 200000 configured), but the user's setting is the
hard ceiling every request must obey. effectiveContextWindow therefore clamps
the learned window to the config again: an observed window only ever shrinks
consumers, never widens them, so the provider-visible context can never
exceed the configured window.

The previous patch made the learned window authoritative, which only worked
after a real 413 overflow had taught it. Preflight already keeps requests
inside the configured window, so the gateway never rejects one, the learned
window never appears, and a session that dwarfs the config deadlocked with
'context is above the maintenance threshold but no foldable region remains':
the fold candidate (digest + retained tail) was always still at or above the
configured physical ceiling, so acceptCheckpointCandidate rejected every
projection.

Fix the deadlock without widening the window:
- foldContext iterates must-free folds (session at/above the hard ceiling)
  until the projection converges below the ceiling; each accepted checkpoint
  strictly shrinks the view, so the loop terminates.
- acceptCheckpointCandidate takes mustFree: an intermediate projection may sit
  above the ceiling as long as it shrinks (foldContext keeps folding it down);
  non-forced maintenance still demands one-shot headroom below the ceiling.
- A fold only counts as success when it lands below the hard ceiling for any
  must-free session; pressure convergence below the fold trigger still counts
  when the view is already safely inside the window.

Also parse the OpenAI-compatible 'input (N tokens) is longer than the model's
context length (M tokens)' overflow and keep the summary request admitted
without clipping its fixed output budget.

Regression tests cover the real-world deadlock with no learned window at all,
the clamped window semantics, and reconciliation with the upstream no-fold
region rule.
