From ee581f8646a622c3879a3f69cd60ac3d403f4cc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:11:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] agent, provider: compaction summaries run with reasoning
 disabled

Summary requests (compact.go summaryRequest) now set provider.Request.NoReasoning.
Every adapter maps it to the endpoint's native off state or drops the
reasoning/effort fields entirely:

- openai: DeepSeek emits thinking.type=disabled with no reasoning_effort;
  MiniMax/GLM/LongCat and generic thinking configs map to thinking.type=disabled;
  Kimi K3 skips its empty-effort "max" ladder; the opencode Zen wire is
  byte-identical (it never carries thinking/effort).
- anthropic: DeepSeek-Anthropic and plain Anthropic emit thinking.type=disabled
  with no output_config.
- responses: DeepSeek maps to reasoning.effort=none; other vendors omit the
  reasoning block.

NoReasoning is host-internal (json:"-", absent from the Extension Protocol
DTO), so extensions never observe it and the wire DTO stays byte-stable.

Tests cover every adapter branch plus the agent->provider contract
(TestSummaryRequest*), including the K3 effort-ladder and opencode identity
regressions.
