From ca31eee0bfe930054efe333cc044d7d0639fe435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/6] openai: disable Zen thinking on DeepSeek compaction summaries

Technically, PATCH 6/6 left deepseek-v4-flash-free (the user's model via the
opencode Zen gateway) unaffected: the opencode wire has no thinking/effort
knob, so NoReasoning changed nothing on the wire and the DeepSeek backend
kept its default thinking-on behaviour.

Fix: for DeepSeek models on the Zen gateway, NoReasoning now carries
DeepSeek's native thinking-off field (thinking.type=disabled) appended
after the CLI-fixed keys. Non-compaction requests stay byte-identical to
the CLI capture, and generic Zen models (e.g. mimo) with no thinking mode
keep the byte-identical body in both directions.

Tests: exact wire strings for the DeepSeek compaction body (fixed key order
plus trailing thinking off) and byte-identity for the default/non-DeepSeek
bodies.
