From: kyehn <kyehn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2026 06:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] agent: fold the dominating active turn on must-free overflow

A physical-overflow fold (must-free at/above the hard input ceiling) can
find no foldable region when the only remaining content is the active
user turn itself: the active-turn protection used to skip it, so
planFoldRegion returned CompactionNoop and every request deadlocked with
"no foldable region remains".

Fold the active turn too on the must-free path when it is the sole
remaining content AND it dominates the visible view (one message already
filling the window). The summary prefix fitter still caps the summary
request below the physical ceiling, so an indivisible message that alone
exceeds the ceiling fails with the precise "no balanced prefix" error
instead of wedging the session. Normal pressure folds and small sessions
keep excluding the active turn, so a too-small window still fails with
ErrCompactionRequired instead of looping summaries.
