From: kyehn <kyehn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 05:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] agent, openai: survive summary requests the backend rejects

Zen free-tier backends reject large summary inputs without usable numbers
("[1261] Prompt exceeds max length", stream EOFs) and reasoning-capable
models (mimo-v2.5-free) can spend the whole summary output budget on
chain-of-thought and return empty content. The trusted ContextLimitError
parser cannot learn from numberless bodies, so every retry resent the
same oversized request and the turn died with ErrCompactionRequired.

- opencode wire: carry NoReasoning as thinking.type=disabled for every
  model on a compaction summary, not only DeepSeek; ordinary traffic keeps
  the byte-identical CLI body.
- foldContext: classify capacity-style summary failures (prompt exceeds /
  too long / unexpected EOF / empty output), halve the learned window via
  learnContextBudget, and refold against the recalibrated ceiling instead
  of failing the turn. The halving stops at a 32k floor; rate limits and
  other non-capacity errors never shrink.
- maximumSafeSummaryPrefixEnd: a learned window below the configured one
  (capacity shrink or gateway overflow) now fits the summary prefix even
  for unknown-window backends that previously sent the fold uncut.
